{
  "_doc": "What Lumi's look is built from (systems/lumi_style.gd). A style is a dict of slots: colour slots (paint, trim, accent, side, eyes, glow, hover, laser) and part slots that pick one option id each. Which of these the player may wear is decided by found pieces alone (data/cosmetics.json: a piece names an option, a swatch or a design's paint set); nothing here carries an unlock rule. Option fields: acc = PatchModel-native add-on names (PatchModel.VARIANTS acc ids, built by PatchModel itself), parts = add-on mesh names looked up in the add-on library (aurora.glb + designs.glb, first one found wins; a procedural fallback named by build is used when none exists). Part slots: pattern (wear pattern and its panels), eye_shape, head (head piece), ears (ear lenses and side pieces), chest (plate icon), shoulders, held (left claw), hip, companion; the first option of a slot is its empty one. swatches: named colours (hex) that paint tins and lens chips refer to. slots: the style's own keys with their kind (the Locker's slot list is data/cosmetics.json slots). The six designs are presets that fill every slot (LumiStyle.preset).",
